  "lines": [
    "----",
    "",
    "",
    "can you make a new neovim plugin for me?",
    "",
    "[`a-empty.txt`](a-empty.txt)",
    "",
    "----",
    "",
    "",
    "I'll help you create a new Neovim plugin. Let me first examine your current setup and then create the plugin structure.",
    "",
    "**󰝖  plan** `4 todos`",
    "- [ ] Examine existing Lua plugin structure ",
    "- [ ] Create basic plugin directory structure ",
    "- [ ] Write main plugin init.lua file ",
    "- [ ] Create plugin documentation ",
    "",
    "----",
    "",
    "",
    "**  read** `/Users/cam/tmp/a/lua/example-plugin/init.lua`",
    "",
    "`````lua",
    "local M = {}",
    "",
    "function M.setup(opts)",
    "  opts = opts or {}",
    "  ",
    "  local config = {",
    "    greeting = opts.greeting or \"Hello from example-plugin!\",",
    "    enable_commands = opts.enable_commands ~= false,",
    "  }",
    "  ",
    "  if config.enable_commands then",
    "    M.create_commands()",
    "  end",
    "  ",
    "  M.config = config",
    "end",
    "",
    "function M.hello()",
    "  print(M.config.greeting)",
    "end",
    "",
    "function M.get_current_line()",
    "  local line = vim.api.nvim_get_current_line()",
    "  print(\"Current line: \" .. line)",
    "  return line",
    "end",
    "",
    "function M.create_commands()",
    "  vim.api.nvim_create_user_command('ExampleHello', function()",
    "    M.hello()",
    "  end, {})",
    "  ",
    "  vim.api.nvim_create_user_command('ExampleCurrentLine', function()",
    "    M.get_current_line()",
    "  end, {})",
    "end",
    "",
    "return M",
    "`````",
    "",
    "----",
    "",
    "",
    "**󰝖  plan** `3 todos`",
    "- [x] Examine existing Lua plugin structure ",
    "- [-] Create basic plugin directory structure ",
    "- [ ] Write main plugin init.lua file ",
    "- [ ] Create plugin documentation ",
    "",
    "----",
    "",
    "",
    "What would you like your Neovim plugin to do? I can see you have an example plugin structure already. I'll need to know:",
    "",
    "1. What functionality you want the plugin to provide",
    "2. What you'd like to name it",
    "3. Any specific features or commands you want to include",
    "",
    "Once you provide these details, I can create a complete plugin structure for you based on the pattern I see in your existing example-plugin.",
    "",
    ""
  ],
